### ========================================
### FLOW TEST - Complete User Journey
### ========================================

### Step 1: Register User A
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alice Johnson",
  "email": "alice@test.com",
  "password": "alice123"
}

### Step 2: Register User B
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bob Smith",
  "email": "bob@test.com",
  "password": "bob123"
}

### Step 3: Login as Alice
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@test.com",
  "password": "alice123"
}

### Step 4: Get Users (Alice)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Step 5: Create Conversation between Alice and Bob
POST {{baseUrl}}/chat/conversations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "direct",
  "participants": ["PASTE_BOB_ID_HERE"]
}

### Step 6: Send Message from Alice
POST {{baseUrl}}/chat/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "conversationId": "PASTE_CONVERSATION_ID_HERE",
  "text": "Hi Bob! This is Alice."
}

### Step 7: Get Messages
GET {{baseUrl}}/chat/messages/PASTE_CONVERSATION_ID_HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Step 8: Update Alice's Profile
PUT {{baseUrl}}/auth/update-profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alice Johnson (Updated)",
  "avatar": "https://picsum.photos/seed/alice/200"
}

### ========================================
### INSTRUCTIONS
### ========================================
### 
### HOW TO USE:
### 
### 1. Start the backend server:
###    cd nexus_chat_backend
###    npm run dev
###
### 2. Copy the token from the login response (Step 3 or 7)
###    and replace {{token}} at the top of this file
###
### 3. For user IDs and conversation IDs:
###    - Run "Get All Users" to get user IDs
###    - Run "Get All Conversations" to get conversation IDs
###    - Replace PASTE_USER_ID_HERE and PASTE_CONVERSATION_ID_HERE
###
### 4. In Rapid Client or VS Code REST Client:
###    - Click "Send Request" above each request
###    - Results will appear in the response panel
###
### 5. Test edge cases by running requests marked with
###    "(Should Fail - Edge Case)" - they should return 400/401/500
###
### 6. Test success cases - they should return 200/201
###
### ========================================
